@startuml LLD: Web Auth - Universal Sequence Diagram
skinparam defaultFontSize 16
skinparam actorStyle hollow
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 120

actor "User" as User
participant "Web Client\n(Storefront or Dashboard)" as Client
participant "Backend for Frontend\n(BFF)" as Bff
box "Application Services" #FFF7ED
participant "Identity Service" as Identity #FDBA74
participant "Protected Service" as Service #FDBA74
end box

note over Client, Service
Storefront accepts customer sessions and may resume the originally requested route.
Dashboard accepts employee sessions and checks permissions for protected features.
Both applications access backend services through their BFF boundary.
end note

== Sign-in and role validation ==
User -> Client : 1.1 Open sign-in page
activate Client
User -> Client : 1.2 Submit credentials
Client -> Bff : 1.3 Authenticate
activate Bff
Bff -> Identity : 1.4 Authenticate credentials
activate Identity

alt Credentials accepted
  Identity --> Bff : 1.4.1.1 Return access and refresh credentials
  deactivate Identity
  Bff --> Client : 1.4.1.2 Return session credentials
  deactivate Bff
  Client -> Client : 1.4.1.3 Validate role required by the application
  alt Role accepted
    Client -> Client : 1.4.1.4.1 Establish session
    Client --> User : 1.4.1.4.2 Continue to the application
  else Role rejected
    Client -> Client : 1.4.1.5.1 Discard session credentials
    Client --> User : 1.4.1.5.2 Show access denial
  end
else Credentials rejected
  Identity --> Bff : 1.4.2.1 Reject authentication
  deactivate Identity
  Bff --> Client : 1.4.2.2 Return authentication failure
  deactivate Bff
  Client --> User : 1.4.2.3 Show sign-in error
end
deactivate Client

newpage Session restoration and route authorization

== Session restoration ==
User -> Client : 2.1 Open a protected route
activate Client
Client -> Client : 2.2 Restore session state

alt Access session is valid
  Client -> Client : 2.2.1.1 Reuse current session
else Session can be renewed
  Client -> Bff : 2.2.2.1 Renew session
  activate Bff
  Bff -> Identity : 2.2.2.2 Renew session credentials
  activate Identity
  alt Renewal accepted and role remains valid
    Identity --> Bff : 2.2.2.3.1 Return renewed credentials
    deactivate Identity
    Bff --> Client : 2.2.2.3.2 Return renewed session
    deactivate Bff
    Client -> Client : 2.2.2.3.3 Update session
  else Renewal rejected or role no longer valid
    Identity --> Bff : 2.2.2.4.1 Reject renewal
    deactivate Identity
    Bff --> Client : 2.2.2.4.2 Return renewal failure
    deactivate Bff
    Client -> Client : 2.2.2.4.3 Clear session
  else Identity service temporarily unavailable
    Identity --> Bff : 2.2.2.5.1 Return temporary failure
    deactivate Identity
    Bff --> Client : 2.2.2.5.2 Return temporary failure
    deactivate Bff
    Client -> Client : 2.2.2.5.3 Preserve renewable session context
  end
else No renewable session exists
  Client -> Client : 2.2.3.1 Continue as anonymous
end

note over Client, Identity
Concurrent browser contexts coordinate renewal.
A temporary service failure does not invalidate an otherwise renewable session.
end note

== Route authorization ==
alt User is not authenticated
  Client --> User : 2.3.1.1 Redirect to sign-in
else Dashboard feature permission is missing
  Client -> Client : 2.3.2.1 Deny the requested feature
  Client --> User : 2.3.2.2 Navigate to a safe application route
else User is authenticated and authorized
  Client --> User : 2.3.3.1 Continue to the requested route
end
deactivate Client

newpage Protected request renewal and logout

== Protected API request ==
User -> Client : 3.1 Trigger a protected action
activate Client
Client -> Bff : 3.2 Send request with access credential
activate Bff
Bff -> Service : 3.3 Forward authenticated request
activate Service

alt Request succeeds or fails for a non-auth reason
  Service --> Bff : 3.3.1.1 Return service response
  deactivate Service
  Bff --> Client : 3.3.1.2 Return response
else Access credential is rejected
  Service --> Bff : 3.3.2.1 Reject access credential
  deactivate Service
  Bff --> Client : 3.3.2.2 Return authentication failure
  Client -> Bff : 3.3.2.3 Renew session
  Bff -> Identity : 3.3.2.4 Renew session credentials
  activate Identity
  alt Renewal succeeds
    Identity --> Bff : 3.3.2.5.1 Return renewed credentials
    deactivate Identity
    Bff --> Client : 3.3.2.5.2 Return renewed session
    Client -> Bff : 3.3.2.5.3 Retry request once
    Bff -> Service : 3.3.2.5.4 Forward request with renewed credential
    activate Service
    Service --> Bff : 3.3.2.5.5 Return service response
    deactivate Service
    Bff --> Client : 3.3.2.5.6 Return retried response
  else Renewal fails
    Identity --> Bff : 3.3.2.6.1 Reject renewal
    deactivate Identity
    Bff --> Client : 3.3.2.6.2 Return renewal failure
    Client -> Client : 3.3.2.6.3 Clear session
  end
end
deactivate Bff
Client --> User : 3.4 Present result
deactivate Client

== Logout ==
User -> Client : 4.1 Sign out
activate Client
Client -> Bff : 4.2 End current session
activate Bff
Bff -> Identity : 4.3 Revoke current session
activate Identity
Identity --> Bff : 4.4 Confirm or report best-effort result
deactivate Identity
Bff --> Client : 4.5 Complete sign-out request
deactivate Bff
Client -> Client : 4.6 Clear local session state
Client --> User : 4.7 Navigate to the signed-out destination
deactivate Client

@enduml
